  "answer": "I found no past ticket that reports this problem. The crash comes from PowerShell, not from Windows Terminal. The stack trace shows pwsh 7.6.6 failing in UpdatesNotification.ShowUpdateNotification. It calls String.PadRight with a negative width (-17), which probably happens because the console window or width is very narrow when pwsh starts. You can work around it by setting the environment variable POWERSHELL_UPDATECHECK=Off, which turns off the update notification. You can also start pwsh with a wider initial window or column count. Another option is to update PowerShell, or to check whether the issue is already open in the PowerShell repository (PowerShell/PowerShell). If you report it there, include the stack trace and your window size settings. The related Terminal settings are initialCols and launchMode."
 },
